 },  
 "cells": \[  
  {  
   "cell\_type": "markdown",  
   "metadata": {},  
   "source": "\# EUR Bond Maturity Monitor — BQL / BQuant\\n\\n\#\# The bug that was producing NaN\\n\\n\`bql.combined\_df()\` outer-joins one frame per requested field. Pure-static fields\\n(\`name\`, \`id\_isin\`, \`crncy\`, \`maturity\`, \`issue\_dt\`, \`cpn\_typ\`) return a frame indexed by ID only.\\nDated or currency-tagged fields (\`cpn\`, \`amt\_outstanding\`, \`nxt\_call\_dt\`, \`industry\_sector\`,\\n\`normalized\_payment\_rank\`) return extra columns — \`AS\_OF\_DATE\`, \`CURRENCY\`, \`REVISION\_DATE\`.\\nThe join keys therefore differ, rows do not line up, and everything in the second group fills NaN.\\n\\nThat is exactly the split you observed, and it is why the Step-3 probe passed: the probe requests\\n\*\*one\*\* field at a time, so there is nothing to misalign.\\n\\n\#\# The fix\\n\\n\*\*One field per query, always.\*\* Two passes:\\n\\n1. \*\*Pass 1\*\* — per issuer, resolve the bond universe and capture BQL's own security IDs.\\n2. \*\*Pass 2\*\* — for each field, one query over those IDs, returning a single Series. Join on ID\\n   in pandas, where we control the join instead of guessing at BQL's.\\n\\nEvery query is single-field, so the misalignment cannot occur. Slower — roughly\\n\`n\_fields x n\_chunks\` queries — and correct, which is the trade you want.\\n\\nRaw output is written to CSV \*\*before\*\* any filtering, so you can inspect exactly what Bloomberg\\nreturned rather than what the notebook did to it afterwards."  
  },  
  {  
   "cell\_type": "code",  
   "metadata": {},  
   "source": "import bql\\nimport pandas as pd\\nimport numpy as np\\nimport warnings, smtplib, os, platform\\nfrom email.mime.text import MIMEText\\nfrom email.mime.multipart import MIMEMultipart\\nfrom IPython.display import display\\n\\nwarnings.filterwarnings('ignore')\\npd.set\_option('display.width', 240)\\npd.set\_option('display.max\_columns', 80)\\n\\nbq \= bql.Service()\\n\\nTODAY      \= pd.Timestamp.now().normalize()\\nTODAY\_STR  \= TODAY.strftime('%Y-%m-%d')\\nBASE\_CCY   \= 'EUR'\\nKEEP\_CCY   \= \['EUR'\]\\nHORIZON\_D  \= 90\\nCRITICAL\_D \= 30\\nMIN\_AMT    \= 0.0\\nID\_CHUNK   \= 150          \# security IDs per query in Pass 2\\nOUT\_DIR    \= '.'          \# CSVs land here, downloadable from the BQuant file browser\\n\\nprint(f'{platform.system()}  ref={TODAY\_STR}  base={BASE\_CCY}  horizon={HORIZON\_D}d')",  
   "outputs": \[\],  
   "execution\_count": null  
  },  
  {  
   "cell\_type": "markdown",  
   "metadata": {},  
   "source": "\#\# Step 1 — Inputs"  
  },  
  {  
   "cell\_type": "code",  
   "metadata": {},  
   "source": "CPTY \= {\\n    'ENEL':'ENEL IM Equity',      'ENI':'ENI IM Equity',        'SNAM':'SRG IM Equity',\\n    'Terna':'TRN IM Equity',      'Italgas':'IG IM Equity',     'Iren':'IRE IM Equity',\\n    'A2A':'A2A IM Equity',        'ERG':'ERG IM Equity',        'Telecom Italia':'TIT IM Equity',\\n    'Stellantis':'STLAM IM Equity','Galp':'GALP PL Equity',     'EDP':'EDP PL Equity',\\n    'REN':'RENE PL Equity',       'Volkswagen':'VOW GR Equity', 'SAP':'SAP GR Equity',\\n    'Bayer':'BAYN GR Equity',     'Fresenius':'FRE GR Equity',  'Linde':'LIN GR Equity',\\n    'E.ON':'EOAN GR Equity',      'Renault':'RNO FP Equity',    'EDF':'EDF FP Equity',\\n    'TotalEnergies':'TTE FP Equity','Telefonica':'TEF SM Equity','Iberdrola':'IBE SM Equity',\\n    'Repsol':'REP SM Equity',     'Philips':'PHIA NA Equity',   'AB InBev':'ABI BB Equity',\\n    'IBM':'IBM US Equity',        'Alphabet':'GOOGL US Equity', 'Verizon':'VZ US Equity',\\n    \\"McDonald's\\":'MCD US Equity', 'Toyota':'7203 JP Equity',\\n}\\n\\n\# counterparty \-\> ISINs pasted from a SRCH \<GO\> export, to cover finance subsidiaries\\nEXTRA\_ISINS \= {\\n    \# 'ENEL': \['XS2576550016', 'XS2325565338'\],\\n}\\n\\nFIELDS \= {\\n    'Name'         : 'name',\\n    'ISIN'         : 'id\_isin',\\n    'Ccy'          : 'crncy',\\n    'Maturity'     : 'maturity',\\n    'IssueDt'      : 'issue\_dt',\\n    'Coupon'       : 'cpn',\\n    'CpnType'      : 'cpn\_typ',\\n    'CpnFreq'      : 'cpn\_freq',\\n    'AmtOutBase'   : f'amt\_outstanding(currency={BASE\_CCY})',\\n    'AmtOutNative' : 'amt\_outstanding',\\n    'AmtIssued'    : 'amt\_issued',\\n    'PayRank'      : 'normalized\_payment\_rank',\\n    'Sector'       : 'industry\_sector',\\n    'Country'      : 'country\_iso',\\n    'Issuer'       : 'issuer',\\n    'NxtCallDt'    : 'nxt\_call\_dt',\\n    'NxtPutDt'     : 'nxt\_put\_dt',\\n    'Callable'     : 'callable',\\n    'Putable'      : 'putable',\\n    'MakeWhole'    : 'make\_whole\_call',\\n}\\nprint(f'{len(CPTY)} counterparties, {len(FIELDS)} fields, '\\n      f'{sum(len(v) for v in EXTRA\_ISINS.values())} supplementary ISINs')",  
   "outputs": \[\],  
   "execution\_count": null  
  },  
  {  
   "cell\_type": "markdown",  
   "metadata": {},  
   "source": "\#\# Step 2 — Single-field query helper\\n\\n\`AUX\` lists the metadata columns BQL bolts onto a value. Anything not in that set is the value\\nitself. This is the whole fix: we extract one clean Series per field and never let BQL join\\nanything for us."  
  },  
  {  
   "cell\_type": "code",  
   "metadata": {},  
   "source": "AUX \= {'DATE','CURRENCY','AS\_OF\_DATE','REVISION\_DATE','PERIOD\_END\_DATE',\\n       'ORDER','ID','INDEX','LEVEL\_0','ITERATION\_DATE'}\\n\\ndef one\_field(expr, alias, univ, verbose=False):\\n    '''Run a SINGLE-field BQL query. Returns (Series indexed by BQL id, error\_string).'''\\n    q \= f'get({expr} as \#{alias}) for({univ})'\\n    try:\\n        d \= bql.combined\_df(bq.execute(q))\\n    except Exception as e:\\n        if verbose: print(f'      \[{alias}\] {type(e).\_\_name\_\_}: {str(e)\[:140\]}')\\n        return None, f'{type(e).\_\_name\_\_}: {str(e)\[:140\]}'\\n    if d is None or len(d) \== 0:\\n        return None, 'empty'\\n    d \= d.copy()\\n    d.index.name \= 'ID'\\n    vals \= \[c for c in d.columns if str(c).strip('\#').upper() not in AUX\]\\n    if not vals:\\n        return None, f'no value column in {list(d.columns)}'\\n    pref \= \[c for c in vals if str(c).strip('\#').lower() \== alias.lower()\]\\n    col  \= pref\[0\] if pref else vals\[0\]\\n    s \= d\[col\]\\n    s \= s\[\~s.index.duplicated(keep='first')\]\\n    return s.rename(alias), ''\\n\\ndef id\_universe(ids):\\n    return '\[' \+ ','.join(f\\"'{i}'\\" for i in ids) \+ '\]'\\n\\n\_s, \_e \= one\_field('name', 'Name', \\"'IBM US Equity'\\")\\nprint('sanity:', 'OK' if \_s is not None else f'FAILED {\_e}')",  
   "outputs": \[\],  
   "execution\_count": null  
  },  
  {  
   "cell\_type": "markdown",  
   "metadata": {},  
   "source": "\#\# Step 3 — Pass 1: resolve the universe\\n\\nOne query per issuer. We keep BQL's own security IDs, because those are guaranteed to resolve as a universe in Pass 2 — unlike reconstructed \`/isin/... Corp\` strings."  
  },  
  {  
   "cell\_type": "code",  
   "metadata": {},  
   "source": "EXPANDER \= \\"debt('{t}')\\"\\n\\nrows, failed \= \[\], \[\]\\nprint('Pass 1 — universe')\\nfor name, tkr in CPTY.items():\\n    univ \= f\\"filter({EXPANDER.format(t=tkr)}, maturity() \> '{TODAY\_STR}')\\"\\n    s, err \= one\_field('id\_isin', 'ISIN', univ)\\n    if s is None:\\n        failed.append(name); print(f'  x  {name:\<16} {err\[:60\]}'); continue\\n    for bid, isin in s.items():\\n        rows.append({'ID': str(bid), 'Counterparty': name, 'IssuerTicker': tkr,\\n                     'ISIN\_p1': isin, 'Source': 'debt()'})\\n    print(f'  ok {name:\<16} {len(s):\>5}')\\n\\nfor name, isins in EXTRA\_ISINS.items():\\n    if not isins: continue\\n    univ \= '\[' \+ ','.join(f\\"'/isin/{x.strip()} Corp'\\" for x in isins) \+ '\]'\\n    s, err \= one\_field('id\_isin', 'ISIN', univ)\\n    if s is None:\\n        print(f'  x  {name:\<16} extra: {err\[:60\]}'); continue\\n    for bid, isin in s.items():\\n        rows.append({'ID': str(bid), 'Counterparty': name,\\n                     'IssuerTicker': CPTY.get(name,''), 'ISIN\_p1': isin, 'Source': 'SRCH'})\\n    print(f'  ok {name:\<16} extra {len(s):\>4}')\\n\\nkeys \= pd.DataFrame(rows).drop\_duplicates(subset='ID').reset\_index(drop=True)\\nALL\_IDS \= keys\['ID'\].tolist()\\nprint(f'\\\\n{len(ALL\_IDS)} unique securities, {keys\[\\"Counterparty\\"\].nunique()} counterparties')\\nprint(f'failed: {failed or \\"none\\"}')\\ndisplay(keys.head())",  
   "outputs": \[\],  
   "execution\_count": null  
  },  
  {  
   "cell\_type": "markdown",  
   "metadata": {},  
   "source": "\#\# Step 4 — Pass 2: one query per field\\n\\nFor each field, the full ID list is queried in chunks and the pieces concatenated into a single\\nSeries. Every query carries exactly one field, so nothing can misalign.\\n\\nThe coverage table it prints is the thing to read: \*\*non-null count per field\*\*. Any field showing\\n0 is genuinely unavailable on this seat — not a join artefact."  
  },  
  {  
   "cell\_type": "code",  
   "metadata": {},  
   "source": "chunks \= \[ALL\_IDS\[i:i+ID\_CHUNK\] for i in range(0, len(ALL\_IDS), ID\_CHUNK)\]\\nprint(f'Pass 2 — {len(FIELDS)} fields x {len(chunks)} chunks \= {len(FIELDS)\*len(chunks)} queries\\\\n')\\n\\nwide, report \= pd.DataFrame(index=pd.Index(ALL\_IDS, name='ID')), \[\]\\nfor alias, expr in FIELDS.items():\\n    parts, errs \= \[\], \[\]\\n    for ch in chunks:\\n        s, err \= one\_field(expr, alias, id\_universe(ch))\\n        if s is not None: parts.append(s)\\n        elif err: errs.append(err)\\n    if parts:\\n        col \= pd.concat(parts)\\n        col \= col\[\~col.index.duplicated(keep='first')\]\\n        col.index \= col.index.map(str)\\n        wide\[alias\] \= col.reindex(wide.index)\\n        nn \= int(wide\[alias\].notna().sum())\\n    else:\\n        wide\[alias\] \= np.nan; nn \= 0\\n    report.append({'alias': alias, 'expr': expr, 'nonnull': nn,\\n                   'pct': round(100\*nn/max(len(wide),1), 1),\\n                   'err': errs\[0\]\[:70\] if errs else ''})\\n    print(f'  {alias:\<14} {nn:\>5}/{len(wide):\<5} {\\"\\" if nn else \\"  \<-- NO DATA\\"}')\\n\\ncov \= pd.DataFrame(report).sort\_values('nonnull', ascending=False).reset\_index(drop=True)\\nprint('\\\\n=== COVERAGE \===')\\ndisplay(cov)\\n\\nraw \= keys.set\_index('ID').join(wide, how='left').reset\_index()\\nif 'ISIN' not in raw.columns or raw\['ISIN'\].isna().all():\\n    raw\['ISIN'\] \= raw\['ISIN\_p1'\]\\nelse:\\n    raw\['ISIN'\] \= raw\['ISIN'\].fillna(raw\['ISIN\_p1'\])\\n\\np\_raw \= os.path.join(OUT\_DIR, f'bonds\_raw\_{TODAY\_STR}.csv')\\np\_cov \= os.path.join(OUT\_DIR, f'bonds\_coverage\_{TODAY\_STR}.csv')\\nraw.to\_csv(p\_raw, index=False); cov.to\_csv(p\_cov, index=False)\\nprint(f'\\\\nwrote {p\_raw}  ({len(raw)} rows, {len(raw.columns)} cols)')\\nprint(f'wrote {p\_cov}')",  
   "outputs": \[\],  
   "execution\_count": null  
  },  
  {  
   "cell\_type": "markdown",  
   "metadata": {},  
   "source": "\#\# Step 5 — Read the CSV back and inspect\\n\\nDeliberately re-read from disk. What you see below is what was actually persisted, not an in-memory object that might have been mutated."  
  },  
  {  
   "cell\_type": "code",  
   "metadata": {},  
   "source": "chk \= pd.read\_csv(p\_raw)\\nprint(f'{len(chk)} rows x {len(chk.columns)} cols\\\\n')\\nprint('non-null per column:')\\nprint(chk.notna().sum().sort\_values(ascending=False).to\_string())\\nprint('\\\\nfirst 8 rows:')\\ndisplay(chk.head(8))",  
   "outputs": \[\],  
   "execution\_count": null  
  },  
  {  
   "cell\_type": "markdown",  
   "metadata": {},  
   "source": "\#\# Step 6 — Normalise"  
  },  
  {  
   "cell\_type": "code",  
   "metadata": {},  
   "source": "b \= chk.copy()\\n\\nfor c in ('Maturity','NxtCallDt','NxtPutDt','IssueDt'):\\n    if c in b: b\[c\] \= pd.to\_datetime(b\[c\], errors='coerce')\\nfor c in ('Coupon','CpnFreq','AmtOutBase','AmtOutNative','AmtIssued'):\\n    if c in b: b\[c\] \= pd.to\_numeric(b\[c\], errors='coerce')\\n\\nn \= len(b); b \= b.dropna(subset=\['ISIN','Maturity'\]).drop\_duplicates(subset='ISIN')\\nprint(f'dedupe:            {n} \-\> {len(b)}')\\n\\nb\['Ccy'\] \= (b.get('Ccy', pd.Series(index=b.index, dtype=object))\\n              .astype(str).str.strip().str.upper()\\n              .replace({'NAN': np.nan, 'NONE': np.nan, '': np.nan}))\\nnc \= int(b\['Ccy'\].isna().sum())\\nif nc: print(f'\!\! {nc} null-currency rows kept, excluded from totals')\\nif KEEP\_CCY:\\n    n \= len(b); b \= b\[b\['Ccy'\].isin(KEEP\_CCY) | b\['Ccy'\].isna()\]\\n    print(f'ccy {KEEP\_CCY}:        {n} \-\> {len(b)}')\\n\\nb\['TTM\_Days'\] \= (b\['Maturity'\] \- TODAY).dt.days\\nn \= len(b); b \= b\[b\['TTM\_Days'\] \> 0\]\\nprint(f'matured dropped:   {n} \-\> {len(b)}')\\n\\nHAS\_BASE \= 'AmtOutBase' in b.columns and b\['AmtOutBase'\].notna().any()\\nb\['Amt'\] \= b\['AmtOutBase'\] if HAS\_BASE else b.get('AmtOutNative', np.nan)\\nif not HAS\_BASE: print('\!\! native amounts only — cross-ccy sums disabled')\\nif 'AmtIssued' in b.columns:\\n    fb \= b\['Amt'\].isna() & b\['AmtIssued'\].notna()\\n    b.loc\[fb, 'Amt'\] \= b.loc\[fb, 'AmtIssued'\]\\n    if fb.any(): print(f'amt\_issued fallback on {int(fb.sum())}')\\nif MIN\_AMT \> 0:\\n    n \= len(b); b \= b\[(b\['Amt'\] \>= MIN\_AMT) | b\['Amt'\].isna()\]\\n    print(f'min amount:        {n} \-\> {len(b)}')\\n\\nif b\['Amt'\].notna().any():\\n    print(f\\"\\\\nunits: median={b\['Amt'\].median():,.0f}  max={b\['Amt'\].max():,.0f}\\")\\n    print('  EUR benchmark \~5e8-1.5e9. If \~5e5-1.5e6 the field is in THOUSANDS.')\\n\\np\_cl \= os.path.join(OUT\_DIR, f'bonds\_clean\_{TODAY\_STR}.csv')\\nb.to\_csv(p\_cl, index=False)\\nprint(f'\\\\nfinal: {len(b)} bonds / {b\[\\"Counterparty\\"\].nunique()} counterparties \-\> {p\_cl}')\\ndisplay(b.head(10))",  
   "outputs": \[\],  
   "execution\_count": null  
  },  
  {  
   "cell\_type": "markdown",  
   "metadata": {},  
   "source": "\#\# Step 7 — Alerts"  
  },  
  {  
   "cell\_type": "code",  
   "metadata": {},  
   "source": "alerts, suppressed \= \[\], \[\]\\nHAS\_MW \= 'MakeWhole' in b.columns and b\['MakeWhole'\].notna().any()\\n\\ndef \_row(r, typ, dt, days, note=''):\\n    return {'Type':typ,'Urgency':'CRITICAL' if days \<= CRITICAL\_D else 'WARNING',\\n            'Counterparty':r\['Counterparty'\],'Name':r.get('Name'),'ISIN':r\['ISIN'\],\\n            'Date':dt,'Days':int(days),'Ccy':r.get('Ccy'),'Amount':r.get('Amt'),\\n            'Coupon':r.get('Coupon'),'PayRank':r.get('PayRank'),\\n            'Src':r.get('Source',''),'Note':note}\\n\\ndef \_truthy(v):\\n    if isinstance(v, str): return v.strip().upper() in ('Y','YES','TRUE','1')\\n    return bool(v) if pd.notna(v) else False\\n\\nfor \_, r in b\[b\['TTM\_Days'\] \<= HORIZON\_D\].iterrows():\\n    alerts.append(\_row(r, 'MATURITY', r\['Maturity'\], r\['TTM\_Days'\]))\\n\\nfor typ, col in (('CALL','NxtCallDt'), ('PUT','NxtPutDt')):\\n    if col not in b.columns: continue\\n    s \= b\[b\[col\].notna()\].copy()\\n    s\['D'\] \= (s\[col\] \- TODAY).dt.days\\n    for \_, r in s\[(s\['D'\] \> 0\) & (s\['D'\] \<= HORIZON\_D)\].iterrows():\\n        if typ \== 'CALL' and HAS\_MW and \_truthy(r.get('MakeWhole')):\\n            suppressed.append(\_row(r, 'CALL\_MAKEWHOLE', r\[col\], r\['D'\])); continue\\n        note \= '' if (typ \== 'PUT' or HAS\_MW) else 'VERIFY IN DES — par vs make-whole unknown'\\n        alerts.append(\_row(r, typ, r\[col\], r\['D'\], note))\\n\\nadf \= pd.DataFrame(alerts); sdf \= pd.DataFrame(suppressed)\\nif len(adf):\\n    adf \= adf.sort\_values(\['Days','Counterparty'\]).reset\_index(drop=True)\\n    p\_al \= os.path.join(OUT\_DIR, f'bond\_alerts\_{TODAY\_STR}.csv')\\n    adf.to\_csv(p\_al, index=False)\\n    print(f\\"{len(adf)} alerts  CRITICAL={(adf\['Urgency'\]=='CRITICAL').sum()}  \-\> {p\_al}\\")\\n    if HAS\_BASE and adf\['Ccy'\].notna().all():\\n        print(f\\"total: {adf\['Amount'\].sum(skipna=True):,.0f} {BASE\_CCY}\\")\\n    else:\\n        print('total: not shown (mixed/unknown currency)')\\n    display(adf)\\nelse:\\n    print('No events in window.')\\nif len(sdf):\\n    print(f'\\\\n{len(sdf)} make-whole calls suppressed'); display(sdf)",  
   "outputs": \[\],  
   "execution\_count": null  
  },  
  {  
   "cell\_type": "markdown",  
   "metadata": {},  
   "source": "\#\# Step 8 — Maturity ladder"  
  },  
  {  
   "cell\_type": "code",  
   "metadata": {},  
   "source": "lad \= b\[b\['TTM\_Days'\] \<= 365\*3\].copy()\\nif len(lad) and lad\['Amt'\].notna().any():\\n    lad\['Bucket'\] \= lad\['Maturity'\].dt.to\_period('Q').astype(str)\\n    piv \= lad.pivot\_table(index='Counterparty', columns='Bucket', values='Amt',\\n                          aggfunc='sum', fill\_value=0)\\n    piv\['TOTAL'\] \= piv.sum(axis=1)\\n    piv \= piv.sort\_values('TOTAL', ascending=False)\\n    piv.to\_csv(os.path.join(OUT\_DIR, f'bond\_ladder\_{TODAY\_STR}.csv'))\\n    try:    display(piv.style.format('{:,.0f}'))\\n    except Exception: display(piv.round(0))\\nelif len(lad):\\n    display(lad.pivot\_table(index='Counterparty', columns=lad\['Maturity'\].dt.to\_period('Q').astype(str),\\n                            values='ISIN', aggfunc='count', fill\_value=0))\\nelse:\\n    print('nothing inside 3y')",  
   "outputs": \[\],  
   "execution\_count": null  
  },  
  {  
   "cell\_type": "markdown",  
   "metadata": {},  
   "source": "\#\# Step 9 — Email"  
  },  
  {  
   "cell\_type": "code",  
   "metadata": {},  
   "source": "ENABLE\_EMAIL    \= False\\nSMTP\_HOST       \= 'smtp.bloomberg.com'\\nSMTP\_PORT       \= 25\\nSENDER\_EMAIL    \= 'you@yourfirm.com'\\nRECIPIENT\_EMAIL \= 'you@yourfirm.com'\\nCC\_EMAILS       \= \[\]\\n\\ndef build\_html():\\n    if not len(adf):\\n        return f'\<p\>No events in the next {HORIZON\_D} days.\</p\>'\\n    cols \= \[c for c in \['Counterparty','Name','ISIN','Type','Date','Days','Ccy',\\n                        'Amount','Coupon','PayRank','Src','Note'\] if c in adf.columns\]\\n    def tbl(d):\\n        if not len(d): return '\<p\>\<i\>none\</i\>\</p\>'\\n        x \= d\[cols\].copy()\\n        x\['Date'\]   \= pd.to\_datetime(x\['Date'\]).dt.strftime('%Y-%m-%d')\\n        x\['Amount'\] \= x\['Amount'\].map(lambda v: f'{v:,.0f}' if pd.notna(v) else '')\\n        return x.to\_html(index=False, border=0).replace(\\n            '\<table','\<table cellpadding=6 style=\\"border-collapse:collapse;font:12px Arial\\"')\\n    crit \= adf\[adf\['Urgency'\]=='CRITICAL'\]; warn \= adf\[adf\['Urgency'\]=='WARNING'\]\\n    thin \= ', '.join(cov.loc\[cov.nonnull \== 0, 'alias'\]) or 'none'\\n    return f'''\<html\>\<body style=\\"font:13px Arial\\"\>\\n    \<h2\>Counterparty Bond Events — {TODAY\_STR}\</h2\>\\n    \<p\>{HORIZON\_D}d window \&middot; {len(b)} bonds \&middot; {len(adf)} events\</p\>\\n    \<h3 style=\\"color:\#b00\\"\>CRITICAL (\&le;{CRITICAL\_D}d) — {len(crit)}\</h3\>{tbl(crit)}\\n    \<h3 style=\\"color:\#b57\\"\>WARNING ({CRITICAL\_D+1}-{HORIZON\_D}d) — {len(warn)}\</h3\>{tbl(warn)}\\n    \<hr\>\<p style=\\"font-size:11px;color:\#777\\"\>Bloomberg BQL, one field per query.\\n    Fields with no data on this seat: {thin}. Issuers failed: {failed or 'none'}.\\n    debt() is entity-scoped — subsidiary paper appears only via EXTRA\_ISINS.\</p\>\\n    \</body\>\</html\>'''\\n\\nhtml \= build\_html()\\nif ENABLE\_EMAIL:\\n    m \= MIMEMultipart('alternative')\\n    m\['Subject'\] \= f'\[Bond Monitor\] {TODAY\_STR} — {len(adf)} events'\\n    m\['From'\] \= SENDER\_EMAIL; m\['To'\] \= RECIPIENT\_EMAIL\\n    if CC\_EMAILS: m\['Cc'\] \= ', '.join(CC\_EMAILS)\\n    m.attach(MIMEText(html, 'html'))\\n    with smtplib.SMTP(SMTP\_HOST, SMTP\_PORT) as s:\\n        s.sendmail(SENDER\_EMAIL, \[RECIPIENT\_EMAIL\]+CC\_EMAILS, m.as\_string())\\n    print('sent')\\nelse:\\n    from IPython.display import HTML\\n    print('preview only'); display(HTML(html))",  
   "outputs": \[\],  
   "execution\_count": null  
  },  
  {  
   "cell\_type": "markdown",  
   "metadata": {},  
   "source": "\#\# If a field still shows 0 in the coverage table\\n\\nThat is now a real answer, not an artefact: the field genuinely has no data for this universe on\\nthis seat. Options, in order of effort:\\n\\n1. Try the DAPI mnemonic as the BQL expression — BQL sometimes accepts both spellings.\\n2. Check one bond by hand in \`FLDS \<GO\>\` to see whether Bloomberg holds the value at all.\\n3. If it is populated in the Terminal but empty in BQL, it is a BQL coverage gap. Fixed income is\\n   where those gaps live — optionality fields especially. That is what File B (blpapi, local\\n   Windows) exists for.\\n\\n\`bonds\_raw\_\*.csv\` holds everything before any filtering, so you can always check whether a value\\nwas lost in the pull or in the cleaning."  
